  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Digital Identity as an Enabler for Development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This programme will support governments to implement trusted, secure and inclusive digital Identification and civil registration systems, informed by international evidence and experience, by supporting the World Bank Group&#x2019;s Identification for Development initiative, known as ID4D, between 2019-2020 to 2024-25. This programme will finance ID4D to, first, produce evidence-based guidance on the preferred approaches for digital identification and illustrate the development value of the systems, second, establish and support global platforms, convening and peer-to-peer exchange to share lessons and experiences of what works and why, and third, provide technical assistance to over 30 governments and regional institutions to support countries to roll-out digital identification and civil registration systems. DFID will also support an independent evaluation of the World Bank Group&#x2019;s ID4D programme during the course of this grant.</narrative>
  </description>
